-- The agreement corpus: small programs that may refuse to answer, each line
-- below that starts "agreement:" a verdict that every surface must give.
-- jl4/tests-agreement runs each case through every surface and checks that
-- it gives core's verdict, and that core gives the one written here.
--
-- Every rule takes an input `pad`, which it does not read. The test gives it
-- a number to have the service evaluate a call on its direct path, and {} to
-- have it evaluate the call through its generated wrapper.
--
-- Two rules that answer TRUE or FALSE and may refuse: one through a
-- definition this file imports, one with a reason of its own as well. Every
-- assignment of a rule's inputs is a case.
--
-- agreement: covered may refuse with ["insurance is not modelled"]
-- agreement: covered {"adult": true, "applicant": true} => answers true
-- agreement: covered {"adult": true, "applicant": false} => refuses "insurance is not modelled"
-- agreement: covered {"adult": false, "applicant": true} => answers false
-- agreement: covered {"adult": false, "applicant": false} => answers false
--
-- agreement: checked may refuse with ["insurance is not modelled", "minors are not modelled"]
-- agreement: checked {"adult": true, "applicant": true} => answers true
-- agreement: checked {"adult": true, "applicant": false} => refuses "insurance is not modelled"
-- agreement: checked {"adult": false, "applicant": true} => refuses "minors are not modelled"
-- agreement: checked {"adult": false, "applicant": false} => refuses "minors are not modelled"

IMPORT insurance

@export whether the applicant is covered
GIVEN adult IS A BOOLEAN
      applicant IS A BOOLEAN
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered IF adult AND `the person is insured` applicant

@export whether the applicant is checked
GIVEN adult IS A BOOLEAN
      applicant IS A BOOLEAN
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE checked IF
    IF adult THEN `the person is insured` applicant
    ELSE REFUSE "minors are not modelled"
